    "science_paraxanthine": {
      "type": "custom-science-paraxanthine",
      "blocks": {
        "content": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "eyebrow": "Our Hero Ingredient",
            "heading": "par·ax·an·thine",
            "text": "<p>Paraxanthine is the primary metabolite your body produces from caffeine and is responsible for many of the benefits people associate with it, including energy, alertness, focus, and mental stamina. When caffeine is consumed, the body breaks it down into several metabolites, with paraxanthine being the most abundant.</p><p>By isolating Paraxanthine, we are able to deliver many of caffeine's positive effects without the same drawbacks people associate with traditional caffeine, like jitteriness, restlessness, and an overly harsh feel. Because paraxanthine has a shorter half-life than caffeine, it clears the body faster and does not stick around the same way. That makes it well suited for later-day use without disrupting sleep the way caffeine often can.</p>"
          }
        },
        "stat_1": {
